  "$comment": "Contract for landing content files (marketing/strategy/2026-07-31-landing-i18n-brief.md). Every locale file must define exactly `keys` as {text, from?, status?} leaves. Human-source locales (source: null) carry text only; translated locales carry from = 12-hex sha256 prefix of the source string (stale detection) and status: mt | mt-reviewed | human. Budgets are in Unicode code points; perLocale overrides exist because German runs ~25% longer and Japanese titles are counted in full-width characters (see marketing/seo/2026-07-31-keyword-research.md §6). Key set mirrors the RU v2 mockup (gridfin.pen «RU v2 — Skeleton», 14 sections). Product artifacts (terminal lines, file trees, PRD headers, gate output) are hardcoded in the build template and are NOT content keys — they are the same in every locale by the honesty rule.",
